Let $$P = \left[ {\matrix{
   { - 30} &amp; {20} &amp; {56}  \cr 
   {90} &amp; {140} &amp; {112}  \cr 
   {120} &amp; {60} &amp; {14}  \cr 

 } } \right]$$ and<br><br> $$A = \left[ {\matrix{
   2 &amp; 7 &amp; {{\omega ^2}}  \cr 
   { - 1} &amp; { - \omega } &amp; 1  \cr 
   0 &amp; { - \omega } &amp; { - \omega  + 1}  \cr 

 } } \right]$$ where <br><br>$$\omega  = {{ - 1 + i\sqrt 3 } \over 2}$$, and I<sub>3</sub> be the identity matrix of order 3. If the <br>determinant of the matrix (P<sup>$$-$$1</sup>AP$$-$$I<sub>3</sub>)<sup>2</sup> is $$\alpha$$$$\omega$$<sup>2</sup>, then the value of $$\alpha$$ is equal to ______________.

